{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "name": "policy_signature",
  "description": "Ed25519 signed-policy verification vectors, shared by both SDKs. TS implementation: sdk/src/proxy/policy-verify.ts (consumed by sdk/tests/unit/policy-verify.test.ts). Python implementation: sdk-python/obsvr/policy_verify.py (consumed by sdk-python/tests/test_policy_verify.py). Every case supplies the rules and approvals AS RECEIVED plus the signature block, and pins whether verification accepts. A rejecting case also pins a substring its reason must contain, so both languages refuse for the SAME cause rather than merely refusing. Verification failure is fail-closed everywhere: the fetched policy is discarded and the last-good policy stays in force. Anti-rollback (issued_at monotonicity) is wiring behavior asserted by the poll-path tests, not a vector here.",
  "canonical_message": "obsvr-policy-v1|<issued_at>|<rules_sha256>|<approvals_sha256>",
  "hashing": "rules_sha256 and approvals_sha256 are sha256 hex over the canonical JSON (recursively sorted keys, compact separators) of the received arrays - the same canonicalization the rules hash uses.",
